From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Creker <TheoFool@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 22:41:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Paper Lab hooks
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The fork's single point of intrusion into the patch system, deliberately minimal.

Only what a plugin cannot do stays here. Commands, HUD, counters, the chunk map
and mobcap reading all live in the PaperLab plugin.

1. Observer mode (io.papermc.paper.lab.ghost.LabGhost) - six sites:
   - ChunkMap.updatePlayerMobTypeMap / updateFailurePlayerMobTypeMap - out of the mobcap census;
   - ChunkMap.isChunkNearPlayer - does not widen the spawn area;
   - ChunkMap.skipPlayer - takes no part in chunk loading;
   - NaturalSpawner.spawnForChunk - does not consume the chunk budget;
   - ActivationRange.activateEntities - does not wake mobs (EAR);
   - LivingEntity.canBeSeenByAnyone - mobs do not target them.
   Simulation distance and affectsSpawning are set from the API and need no patch.

2. Spawn trace (io.papermc.paper.lab.spawn.SpawnTrace) - marks in NaturalSpawner:
   hit the cap, attempt started, position rejected, cancelled by a plugin, spawned.
   The engine publishes none of this outwards.

3. Bots (io.papermc.paper.lab.bot) - two lines:
   - MinecraftServer.tickChildren after tickConnection(): the bot's doTick in the
     same phase and the same order relative to tick() as a live player
     (levels -> connection -> players). A plugin cannot do this: its scheduler runs
     at the start of tickChildren, before the level phase;
   - Commands: registration of /player. The command uses vanilla argument types
     (Vec3Argument, RotationArgument, DimensionArgument, GameModeArgument), so it
     lives next to the bots rather than in the plugin.

4. PlayerList.remove - clear observer mode on quit.

Trace collection switches on only while a subscription is active: the hot path is
left with a single volatile field read.

